      "severity": 1,
      "explanation": "Facilities would establish operating limits, tune air assist, and perform inspections, but the proposal retains records, reporting, and agency oversight.",
      "evidence": [],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to specify verification and audit expectations for self-established limits."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "constraint_sequencing_capture",
      "flaw_name": "Constraint Sequencing Capture",
      "defect_type": "Type I",
      "severity": 1,
      "explanation": "Testing and monitoring conditions can determine whether a facility may operate without retesting or additional controls, but this is an ordinary compliance sequence rather than a demonstrated capture mechanism.",
      "evidence": [],
      "comment_leverage": "Request transition examples and cure rules for test-condition disagreements."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "evidence_to_intrusion_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Evidence-to-Intrusion Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The proposal would impose or revise detailed testing, monitoring, recordkeeping, and air-assist controls while the available record leaves questions about whether selected tests represent all affected designs and loading scenarios.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "C-11 and C-12",
          "quote_or_absence": "The notice asks whether additional operating and test data are available for different air-assisted thermal oxidation designs and whether a 400 F default would ensure continuous compliance across design configurations."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Request design-stratified validation and a narrower, performance-based alternative where a universal default is not supported."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "remedy_rationale_mismatch",
      "flaw_name": "Remedy-Rationale Mismatch",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 2,
      "explanation": "The proposal seeks burden relief while asserting no emissions impact, so the final record must show why each revised compliance mechanism is sufficient to preserve control performance rather than merely reduce paperwork or retesting.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "section": "Executive Summary and Section IV",
          "quote_or_absence": "The proposal says the amendments do not change emission-limit stringency and will have no impact on air quality, while changing monitoring and operating provisions."
        }
      ],
      "comment_leverage": "Ask EPA to link each relief provision to an emission-performance demonstration and explain residual risk."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "implementation_fantasy",
      "flaw_name": "Implementation Fantasy",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 1,
      "explanation": "The rule recognizes operational complexity, but it may still assume that facilities can consistently apply loading-condition, air-assist, NHV, and mid-stack-temperature requirements across varied designs.",
      "evidence": [],
      "comment_leverage": "Submit operational data on mixed loading, weather, equipment configuration, and daily inspection feasibility."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "magic_interface_dependency",
      "flaw_name": "Magic Interface Dependency",
      "defect_type": "Type II",
      "severity": 1,
      "explanation": "The proposal depends on measurement methods, data intervals, and control-device interfaces working together reliably, but the available record does not fully document interoperability across the fleet.",
      "evidence": [],
      "comment_leverage": "Request method-validation and data-quality requirements for each monitoring interface."
    },
    {
      "flaw_key": "threat_ambiguity",
